# Minima Rules

- Send Minima RPC commands as a single percent-encoded URL path, not query parameters: build `megammrsync action:resync host:megammr.minima.global:9001`, then call `http://minima:9005/megammrsync%20action%3Aresync%20host%3Amegammr.minima.global%3A9001`.
- Do not expose a generic Minima command proxy. Add a narrow, allowlisted backend action per supported command.
- **RPC console** (`minima-console.catalog.ts`, `minima-console.service.ts`) is the one scoped exception: it runs only commands that are in the static catalog and enabled in the admin whitelist (`GET`/`POST /api/minima/console/whitelist`, re-auth required to edit).
  - Hard-exclude anything that can expose or accept raw keys or seed phrases, or halt the node with no UI recovery: `vault`, `sendfrom`, `signfrom`, `createfrom`, `postfrom`, `createtokenfrom`, `decryptbackup`, `keys`, `quit`. They are not offered at all.
  - Read-only entries default enabled; anything that mutates funds, chain, config, network, or wallet defaults disabled. Classify per argument shape, not per verb: a mutating `action:` form gets its own default-disabled entry listed before the read entry, matching every `action:` outside an explicit read allowlist. See ADR 0015.
  - Where a dedicated action exists (`megammrsync` → `resyncMegammr()`, `peers action:addpeers` → `addMinimaPeers()`, `backup` → `createBackup()`, `restoresync` → `restoreBackup()`), the console dispatches to it rather than re-implementing the RPC.
- **Resync** (`minima-resync.service.ts`, wrapper `resyncMegammr()`): persist the bounded, redacted operation before scheduling the RPC; `POST` returns 202 and admin-only `GET /api/minima/resync` reads progress without node RPC. Ownership is independent of the legacy display marker and only released by reconciliation or definite rejection, checked by operation ID. Restart/backup/restore reserve against resync for their pending work. Never replay resync or force a restart on transport timeout, infer completion from healthy RPC, or add a global mutation queue. The browser polls the progress DTO (3 s busy, 30 s idle) and never parses completion text or sends a recovery restart. See ADR 0034; QA evidence in `docs/reports/536-resync-end-to-end.md`.
- **Backups** (`minima-backup.service.ts`, `/api/minima/backups*`): one stored, encrypted backup password for every backup; re-auth to set, change, or remove it, and to download or restore. Removing it disables automatic backups. One rolling list capped at `MAX_BACKUPS` (20). Restore always uses `restoresync`; plain `restore` and `reset` stay console-only. Automatic backups come from our own nightly scheduler (`minima-backup-scheduler.service.ts`, 00:30 container time, `TZ`), never Minima's `backup auto:true`. See ADR 0037.
- `${MINIMA_DATA_DIR}/backups` is mounted into **both** containers: `backend` read-write at `/minima-backups` (the only shared Minima directory) and `minima` at `/home/minima/backups`. Both mounts are required; see ADR 0037.
- **Automatic node restart** (`/api/minima/restart/auto`, opt-in, every 48 h on the nightly tick) is currently disabled: the scheduler call and the settings toggle are commented out until automations handle a restart mid-run. Keep its settings, routes, and service functions. See ADR 0037.
- **Restart** (`POST /api/minima/restart`) is graceful: `quit compact:true` first (a wrapped internal use; `quit` stays out of the console), detect the cycle from Docker `RestartCount`/`StartedAt` against a pre-`quit` baseline, wait up to 5 minutes, then fall back to a forceful restart. It runs in the background and responds `{ state: "restarting" }` immediately. See ADR 0001.
